WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.560
MAY 13, 2021

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.560
Thank you for your hard work.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.690
Yeah, yeah. Good work.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.730
Tomorrow is the GourFes event.
Counting on you.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.780
Mr. Tarki.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.740
We bought out the brand of cabbage
that Itadaki uses.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.110
They won't be able to make anything tomorrow.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.950
Oh, did you now?

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:24.040
Could you please stop wasting our budget?
The outcome has already been decided.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.790
MAY 14, 2021

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.430
Kozue.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.970
Want to come by today's GourFes?

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.010
It's going to be amazing this year.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.720
The winning shop will collaborate
with convenience stores across the country,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.730
and it's hosted
by the famous comedian KODA-GEN.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:49.360
All right.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.530
I'll wait as long as it takes.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.820
Well, I'll be going now.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.030
All right. Take care.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.080
My ego, huh?

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.220
Kinako is going, too.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.720
THIRD ANNUAL
GOURMET FESTIVAL
2021

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.220
Today is finally the day of GourFes.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.220
I'm gonna eat a ton.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:22.220
Wait.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.390
Is he doing that again?

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:30.940
He does it.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.400
- Ran, with the world record.
- Geez, you're so energetic in the morning.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.150
For little ol' me, it's still late night at 30:00.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:41.780
Ran. I'm always telling you
to please not swim in our bathtubs.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:42.660
Yeah.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:44.910
<i>Ran's naked body.</i>

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.790
Oh no, wait, that's not what I mean, but still...

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.130
I'm glad the Mari-Special menu made it in time.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.340
Yup.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.800
Hot. So hot.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.510
But this is too wonderful!

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.760
Hey, RGB, it's almost time!

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.020
- Yeah.
- Roger that.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.560
Here goes.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.690
I'm full of spirit now!

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.190
Let's go, RGB.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.530
We're gonna use
the convenience store collab prize

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.610
to get the entire country
to know about Takara Shopping Street.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.240
I'm definitely going to get the Grand Prize!

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.540
All the cabbage has been bought out?

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.300
After all that effort of buying them all...

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.930
We'll never understand how Mr. Tarki thinks.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.890
Looks like they'll put it on sale tomorrow.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.640
Gutter and Chop from Yabusame.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.900
They're the land sharks who are trying
to buy out Takara Shopping Street.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.980
Damn it, they're causing trouble again.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.190
Mon Jungle is definitely guilty.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:24.820
Oh man. I'm looking around,
but every market says it's sold out.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.450
Itadaki's okonomiyaki
doesn't use just regular cabbage.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.830
That sweetness only comes out
when you use Midori-Hime.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:35.580
It's a specific brand. There are limits
on how much is out in the market.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.460
At this rate, it'll be like white bread
with no yeast in it.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.090
That's going a bit too far.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:43.260
Hey, wait up, Ran.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.930
What are you planning to do
with a rod that looks like a crowbar?

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.180
Treasure hunting?

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.430
That's a crime.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:52.520
If such a huge amount of cabbage rots,
the farmers will all cry.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.310
Don't change the conversation topic.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.730
I'm affiliated with a police organization.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.480
I can't overlook illegal activity.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.900
We should consult a GourFes
executive committee mem—

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.820
We don't have time for that.
The sun will set before that happens.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.490
Stop it, both of you.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.450
You guys keep telling me to grow up, but...

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.040
That's because you keep
dragging the issue about Asumi.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.370
What about you guys?
You don't care about Asumi at all?

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.370
What was that? There's no way—

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.510
KABA

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.510
Oh, it's just Kaba.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.380
- Hello, Kinako?
- Tsuzuragawa? What's up?

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.590
Hello, Kaba?

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:32.310
<i>I heard from Sakuragi.
You can't get a hold of any cabbages?</i>

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.850
This is it!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.060
Sorry to trouble you. You're a lifesaver.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.400
Thank you so much.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.770
Oh, it's fine.
After all, it's a request from Mr. Kaba.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.150
You knowing so many people
really helped us out.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.450
All of them are getting tired of being beaten
by Takara Mall.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.950
They really want Itadaki to win the Grand Prize.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:56.080
But still, is it okay for you to side with us
as a member of the executive committee?

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.750
I'm not siding with you.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.250
You guys should enter the contest
fair and square.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.500
I can't allow foul tactics
as a committee member, nor as a decent human.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.260
Nothing less from you, Kaba.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:07.800
You get carried away in times like this.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:11.600
Hey, Shuta.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.060
I know that you guys are all capable guys.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:19.190
But when push comes to shove,
you can rely on adults.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.650
Yeah.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.400
But...

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.280
I don't want to trouble you again.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.780
- Come on. What's wrong? This isn't like you.
- Stop it.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:30.820
Sheesh.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:35.240
You do what you believe is just,
and not regret whatever the result may be.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.910
Isn't that right, Shuta?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:44.590
<i>We will now begin the Third Gourmet Festival.</i>

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:49.130
<i>Now, eat, eat up,
and eat to your heart's content.</i>

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.050
Thank you RGB.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.300
Yes.

00:06:58.730 --> 00:06:59.640
All right.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.310
I'll cook up a storm!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:09.700
OKONOMIYAKI
ITADAKI

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.980
- Please line up here.
- We will begin sales very soon.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.740
Okay, two Mari-Specials.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.070
AOI BAKERY

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.490
Got to hand it to the defending champion.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.370
I didn't think my own son would betray us.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.080
It just happened to end up this way.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:20.000
W-Welcome.
Hey dear, we have a customer.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.540
You should help out your own family!

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:27.000
MON JUNGLE

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:22.960
- Come on, don't break our line.
- Here's one monja.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.130
- You sure look like you want to eat some monja.
- Please decide on your order beforehand.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.720
The okonomiyaki from Itadaki
is simply the best.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:54.070
Oh, are you going out?
Are you heading to GourFes?

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.240
I'm sure your father will be happy about that.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:07:59.330
Kinako.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.170
I just want to see Kinako.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.080
MON JUNGLE

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.080
Delicious!

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.460
You just gotta have okonomiyaki in 24th Ward.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.130
Itadaki's variation is so unique.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:14.890
Mon Jungle's flavor feels like
it was written in a manual, you know?

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.350
What was that?

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:19.350
Damn it, how were they able
to get some cabbages?

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.350
This is... unsightly.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.230
Mr. Tarki.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:28.860
No need to fret. The outcome
has already been decided.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:35.030
All right, it's almost time to count the ballots!

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:41.160
Which shop will earn the Grand Prize
for the honorable Third Gourmet Festival?

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:44.170
Okay, here you go. Thanks for coming.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:44.960
See you.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.130
Good work. That was the last one, right?

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.630
I did it. I pulled it off.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.010
There were so many customers here.
I think you got this one.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.220
We have a full row of ballot boxes here.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:01.350
Each of them contain chopsticks
that all of you voted with.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.850
The weight of the boxes
will determine the champion,

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:06.980
KODA-GEN! I've been waiting for you!

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:08.940
and the winning shop will get a collaboration menu
sold in convenience stores all over the country.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.030
A true honor of being the face of 24th Ward.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:17.280
Now, we'll begin
with Entry number 1, Takoyaki King.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:20.280
Whoa, that's 6,562 grams!

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.200
Oh, they got quite a good score.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:28.210
Itadaki's score is overwhelming,
so there's at least double that.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.590
You guys are so easygoing.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.670
If you don't do anything, Itadaki might lose.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.220
Chikuwa.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:39.050
I don't understand. No matter what you think,
Itadaki has the tast—

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:42.010
Taste doesn't matter.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.180
You know something?

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:44.020
Mr. Chikushi.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:47.980
Hey, Koki. You're enjoying your day off.
Makes me jealous.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.190
I was called out to do some security.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.400
Anyways.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:56.150
Yeah. I overheard something yesterday
while checking the venue I'd be working at.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:00.530
So you caught on
to how we doctored up the ballot box.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.620
Is your aim to buy out Takara Shopping Street?

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.910
By winning GourFes you aim to make
Takara Mall the new landmark,

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:09.670
and completely crush the Shopping Street.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:14.420
Is this a ploy to make money
once we're incorporated into Tokyo in six months?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.300
You haven't changed, Hajime Taki.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:22.680
Old places just get in the way
of redevelopment, Hiroki Shirakaba.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:26.230
Tampering with the ballot box
is against the rules.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:28.730
I will have Mon Jungle disqualified.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.650
But can you do that?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:34.320
I've already won over
most of the executive committee.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.440
Even if you alone file a complaint...

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.320
What was that?

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.570
Besides, I hear that your daughter Kozue
refuses to go to school.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:46.250
Out-of-ward school attendance permits
aren't issued all that easily.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:49.790
What a shame, since she had good grades.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.380
All things considered, it seems hard for her
to continue attending her current school.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.260
It takes one to know one.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:01.760
I do have quite a bit of clout. I can help you.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:07.770
Are you all right making your family unhappy
just for your own sense of justice and ego?

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:09.690
Damn that Yabusame.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:11.230
That's totally a threat.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.190
That's right. And you just let it go?

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:16.940
Come on now.
SARG's role is to uphold the peace,

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.490
but we're outsiders
when it's something internal about GourFes.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:24.450
Besides, who can blame a father
for thinking about his daughter?

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:30.120
The fact that they're not disqualified yet
means he handled the situation as an adult.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:31.290
No way that would happen.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.170
Kaba cares about Kozue more than anything.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:38.630
But even so,
he won't twist his own convictions.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:42.800
Next, we have the new hope of 24th Ward.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:46.930
It's now the monjayaki shop,
Mon Jungle's turn!

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:51.390
Whoa. This is heavy. So heavy.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.980
And now, let's weigh it.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:55.650
Excuse me.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:59.610
- Um, Mr. Shirakaba?
- Oh my.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.530
Take a look at this.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:07.790
Mon Jungle was being dishonest,
and planted weights into the ballot box.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:09.790
Therefore, they will be disqualified.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.620
How foolish.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.670
Oh, he does it at this point in time?

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:16.710
Yeah!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:20.710
They can't make excuses now.
Good going, Kaba.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.590
There's no way that Mon Jungle
can recover from this.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:27.220
They say that evil
has never flourished in this world.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:36.980
ASUMI

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.360
A-Asumi?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:55.460
The Grand Prize winner
of the Third Gourmet Festival is...

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.670
Itadaki, the okonomiyaki shop!

00:12:58.670 --> 00:12:59.920
All right.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.090
Thank you, everyone.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:11.140
The crowd panics
from the approaching tornado.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:15.640
If someone moves,
everyone will immediately follow suit.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:18.400
You have only one chance
to call out for an evacuation.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.860
You have two choices.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:28.450
If you escape from the bridge before it's blocked
by the tornado, the weak will be left behind.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:36.830
If you protect the weak inside a cargo container,
the courageous will be sacrificed.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:44.510
No matter which you choose,
you cannot avoid having casualties.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.340
Guide the future.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:55.640
Hey.

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:57.600
- I know.
- Yeah.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.480
A phone call from Asumi.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:04.490
Once again, it's a two-choice trolley dilemma.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:10.570
A tornado? Even if our abilities are enhanced,
how do we deal with a natural phenomenon?

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.160
It's just like last time.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.250
A future that breaks through two choices...

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.960
...is what we have to create.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:21.710
<i>The bottleneck for the evacuation
is the traffic jam on the bridge.</i>

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:26.470
<i>To avoid a tragedy,
we need to clear out the top of the bridge.</i>

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.840
- Shuta. Move all the cars off the bridge.
- Shu. Can you move all the cars off the bridge?

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:33.010
S-Sure.
You guys have some sort of plan, huh?

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.770
Mon Jungle is cheap,
but it tastes a bit lackluster.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.770
Mr. Chikushi, do you have a moment?

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.400
Someone from the security agency was asking
about controlling the traffic after the festival.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.440
Yeah, I'll be right over.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.110
Things are surprisingly rowdy.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:48.650
Yeah, there was a hero of justice
punishing the villains.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:50.030
Yes, right. Then...

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.370
Mr. Shirakaba.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:52.700
What's up?

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:53.580
Sir.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:57.200
A tornado will be hitting this venue soon.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:58.660
T-Tornado?

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:01.790
- I don't see anything like that.
- Hazard Cast is malfunctioning.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.500
We need an evacuation order
as soon as possible.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.590
However...

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:08.840
<i>Approaching with sincerity
is the fastest way to get to Mr. Shirakaba.</i>

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:13.300
I don't want to repeat the tragedy
of Takara Elementary School ever again.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.310
I beg you.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.560
All right. I get it.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:24.820
<i>I'll rescue as many people as I can
by evacuating them across the bridge.</i>

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.480
<i>I'll save more people
than what I saw in that Vision.</i>

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:29.200
Kinako.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:32.450
Huh? What's wrong, Ran?

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:34.120
A tornado will be coming shortly.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.160
Gather everyone around you
and hide inside a cargo container.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.580
TACOS

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.580
A cargo container? What do you mean...

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:40.830
Please!

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:45.960
<i>If people evacuate in the cargo containers,
the people inside will be saved.</i>

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:50.720
<i>But there aren't that many food stalls,
and not a lot of places for people to evacuate.</i>

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:52.680
<i>That means...</i>

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:58.470
<i>I need to access the traffic system,
and get all the empty cargo trailers in operation,</i>

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.850
<i>and gather them all to this parking lot.</i>

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.020
I'll create an evacuation center with my art.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.360
Inability to protect the weak isn't allowed here.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.490
I wonder where Dad is.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:16.280
Old fashioned, French cruller,
strawberry custard French,

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.370
honey-dipped, sugar glazed, chocolate ring....

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:30.380
Tsuzuragawa.
I was just thinking about calling you.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:34.090
<i>Mr. Koki, by any chance,
is there an anomaly happening over there?</i>

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:36.100
<i>Did something come up on Hazard Cast?</i>

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.260
Yes. Something like that.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.980
<i>Make arrangements
for as many ambulances as possible.</i>

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.020
<i>We might have a catastrophe to deal with.</i>

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.230
Understood.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.030
All right.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:53.570
Everyone, please get out of your cars.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.200
Wh-What?

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.660
This is footage
captured by the surveillance cameras.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.910
Hana. Kaoru. We're gonna move out
to the bridge immediately.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:01.540
Okay.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:05.790
Um, everyone, please calm down and listen.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:09.670
Hazard Cast is having some trouble
and the notification has been delayed,

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:13.170
but a tornado will be forming
at this venue very soon.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:18.100
Everyone, please begin your evacuations.
Please distance yourself from this island!

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.260
A tornado?

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:22.060
- Is that really gonna come?
- Hazard Cast is having trouble?

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:27.520
<i>They won't start moving right away,
but they do feel uneasy. Just one more push.</i>

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.940
Look. The SARG guys are already evacuating.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:33.070
Huh? Is someone calling for us?

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.360
- Shut up and run.
- Okay!

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.320
Run!

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.740
M-Me, too.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.040
L-Let's go.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:47.670
<i>Considering the weight of the cargo trailers,
they'll get carried away by the tornado.</i>

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.540
<i>I need some way to counter the wind, yeah?</i>

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.090
Hey, you there! What are you doing?

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:02.470
The bridge is gonna get clogged because cars
are parked here, and that'll create a big mess.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:04.810
Oh, you don't get it.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.440
Like I would.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:09.730
Mr. Chikushi, this guy's no good.
Let's arrest him.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:11.400
- Hana?
- Whoa, Senpai, calm down.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.240
- Hana, this is not the time.
- Let's calm down. Shuta, you stay put, too.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:17.820
Good. Now we'll be able
to save more people this way.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:23.160
I want to know why,
so let's go to security HQ for now.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.160
- I'm telling you.
- You're being too lenient.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.170
<i>Why did you bring the festival attendees?</i>

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.790
<i>Crap, it's gonna crash.</i>

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:42.600
Stop!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:52.060
That was close.

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:09.920
The tornado.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.460
What the hell are you doing?

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:14.170
That's my line. Why did you do this?

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.880
People will be left behind even if you run.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.590
The right answer is to bring over cargo trailers
and take cover inside them.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:25.140
How can you do something so irresponsible
when you can't guarantee safety?

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:28.390
Maximizing the number of people
who can get away and—

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:29.810
Stop it!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.480
This is no time to be arguing.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:34.270
Is this commotion all your doing, RGB?

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:36.150
Kaba.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:47.750
Don't give up!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.330
I'm always telling you guys!

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.330
You can rely on adults.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.800
I'll show you just how awesome adults can be.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:03.220
Brace yourselves, RGB.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:06.260
If all three of you are together,
anything is possible.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:07.220
Isn't that right?

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:08.640
Yeah!

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:12.900
Everyone, keep pushing!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:18.070
Everyone,
please follow our guidance to survive.

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:20.360
Hurry inside the containers.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:28.370
Shu. Ko. Link the trailers together with this
to counter the wind.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:29.750
There's no time!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.410
You need to get into the containers soon, too.

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:36.790
The people left behind...

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.170
Damn it.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:50.310
Damn it, there isn't a future
where we can save everyone?

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:53.850
Someone... Help...

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:54.900
Kozue?

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:56.400
Kaba!

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.020
Is Kozue here?

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.030
What are you saying? There's no way...

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.860
Look, over there!

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.200
Kozue?

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.370
Kozue!

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:11.250
Kaba!

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:14.000
Wait, Shu. You need to put a wire on.

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:16.460
Kozue!

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.000
D-Dad?

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.550
I'll be right there.

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:25.760
Dad!

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.220
Kozue.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:32.470
Dad.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:35.900
You came out here.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:37.810
Thank you.

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:41.190
Unfortunately, the festival has been cancelled.

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:43.280
Now, let's go home.

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:49.200
Kaba! Kozue!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:53.450
Go, Shu.

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:54.830
It's fine. They'll make it in time.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:58.290
Kaba!

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.540
Shuta?

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:01.630
Kozue! Take Kozue!

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:09.850
Damn it!

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:15.100
Shu, the wire can't go any...

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:21.730
Ka...

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:40.460
Kaba!

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:53.140
<i>A tragedy suddenly befell onto a holiday event.</i>

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:58.640
<i>A tornado quickly formed and assaulted
the venue of the Gourmet Festival.</i>

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:58.640
21 PEOPLE DEAD, 130 SERIOUSLY INJURED

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:05.230
<i>At this point in time, we have confirmed
21 fatalities, and over 130 seriously wounded.</i>

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:07.440
<i>According to the announcement
from the meteorological bureau,</i>

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:11.410
<i>the size of the tornado that formed
had created winds over 80 kmh.</i>

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:10.870
It's because we didn't choose.

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:15.160
To run using the bridge,
or to hide in the containers.

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:17.290
We were able to choose a future.

00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:20.420
We should've chosen the path
that was more certain.

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:24.250
No. We should've cooperated
and aimed to create a different future.

00:23:24.550 --> 00:23:26.420
In the end, what happened to Kaba?

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:32.180
It was us. We killed Mr. Shirakaba.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.560
<i>Choose your future.</i>

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:40.730
<i>Choose your destiny.</i>

00:23:42.060 --> 00:23:43.110
What is this?

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:44.480
Is the TV broken?

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:47.740
<i>Hello there, everyone in the 24th Ward.</i>

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:52.200
<i>Did you enjoy that tornado show?</i>

00:23:52.870 --> 00:23:55.160
<i>My name is Carneades.</i>

00:23:55.280 --> 00:23:59.080
<i>I am the one who will thrust choices
upon the world for the future.</i>
